  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Given $\\underset{\\sim}{a}=6i-j$ and $\\underset{\\sim}{b}=-2i+4j$, find the ratio $r:s$ if $r\\underset{\\sim}{a}+s\\underset{\\sim}{b}=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No defined ratio exists; the only solution is $r=s=0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}r(6i-j)+s(-2i+4j)&=0\\\\6ri-rj-2si+4sj&=0\\\\(6r-2s)i+(-r+4s)j&=0\\end{aligned}$$\nEquate both components:\n$$\\begin{aligned}6r-2s&=0\\\\s&=3r\\\\-r+4s&=0\\\\-r+4(3r)&=0\\\\11r&=0\\\\r&=0\\\\s&=0\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $r:s$ is undefined. The source answer $1:3$ satisfies only the $i$-component equation.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
